2. Definitions

"Basic Features" means every function included in this copy of the Software
other than Quantification and PowerPoint-to-MyWB import. "PowerPoint-to-MyWB
import" means both the "Paste MyWB from PowerPoint" function and the "Import
MyWB from PowerPoint File" function. Basic Features include, without
limitation, Marker/Blot View, SVG Preview, Copy SVG for PowerPoint, and the
normal ability to open and save supported MyWB files. A Basic Feature in this
copy will not later be redesignated as a Premium Feature for this copy.

"Premium Features" means functions for which Premium Access is required.
Quantification and PowerPoint-to-MyWB import are the only Premium Features in
this copy of the Software.

"Premium Access" means a current authorization to use one or more Premium
Features, whether provided at no charge or through a separately agreed paid
subscription or other paid license.

3. License grant

Subject to these terms, permission is granted to download, install, and use
the Basic Features for lawful personal, academic, and internal research
purposes without a license fee.

While the Software has valid Premium Access, permission is also granted to use
the Premium Features covered by that authorization for the same permitted
purposes. Premium Access provided at no charge grants the same permission for
its covered Premium Features as paid Premium Access. Paid Premium Access is
subject to the separately agreed paid terms.

You may copy the Software only as necessary to install, use, or back up the
Software for your own permitted use. No other rights are granted.

4. Premium designation and advance notice

Premium Access for Quantification and PowerPoint-to-MyWB import is currently
provided without a subscription fee. No end date for this access at no charge
is scheduled as of the effective date of this license. If the copyright holder
schedules an end to access to either Premium Feature at no charge for this
copy, the copyright holder will provide at least 90 days' advance notice before
paid Premium Access is required.

A function first introduced in a later release may be identified as a Premium
Feature from the time it is introduced. A later release may also be offered
under different license terms. Before a function that is a Basic Feature in
this copy is changed into a Premium Feature in a later release, the copyright
holder will provide at least 90 days' advance notice. Such a change does not
alter the status of that function as a Basic Feature in this copy.

The notice will identify the affected feature, the effective date, and the
available means of continued access. Notice will be published on the official
MyWB release page and may also be delivered through the Software when it
connects to an online service.

The official MyWB release page is:
https://github.com/MasaakiU/MyWB-releases

5. Effect of unavailable Premium Access

If Premium Access is invalid, expires, or does not cover a Premium Feature,
the Software may disable the affected Premium interface and access through
that interface to its saved state.

Loss of Premium Access does not disable the Basic Features. It does not
delete, encrypt, remotely modify, or transfer your local files. The basic
ability to open and save supported MyWB files remains available, although
Premium-specific data or controls may remain unavailable until Premium Access
is restored.

6. License verification and privacy

A successful online verification is required before Premium Features can be
used for the first time and at least once every 30 days afterward to maintain
uninterrupted access. After a successful verification, the Software may cache
an authorization that permits offline use for up to 30 days. That period may
be shorter if a previously announced change to access takes effect sooner. If
the cached authorization expires before verification succeeds, Premium
Features may remain unavailable until a new authorization is obtained.

Information processed in connection with license verification is described in
the Privacy Policy distributed with the Software.

7. Paid subscriptions and automatic renewal

Premium Access provided at no charge does not, by itself, enroll you in a paid
subscription or authorize any charge. Accepting this license or using Premium
Access at no charge is not consent to future billing.

The copyright holder may separately offer an automatically renewing
subscription for Premium Access. A paid subscription may begin only after you
are shown the total price, including applicable taxes where required, billing
interval, first charge date, automatic-renewal terms, cancellation method, and
the effect of cancellation, and you separately and affirmatively agree to those
paid terms through a purchase action that clearly communicates the obligation
to pay.

After that agreement, the subscription may renew and charges may recur until
you cancel in accordance with the paid subscription terms. If a separately
offered free trial will convert to a paid subscription, the first charge date
and price must be disclosed and agreed to when that trial is accepted.

For an online subscription, a reasonably accessible online cancellation
method and a retainable confirmation of the agreed paid terms will be
provided. A record of the paid-terms version, consent date and time, displayed
price, and billing interval will be maintained. Applicable consumer rights and
mandatory law are not limited by this license.

